# Git

## Safety

- Commit only when the user asks.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, keys, tokens).
- No force-push `main` unless explicitly requested.

## Commits

- Conventional commits, module id as scope when applicable:
  `feat(m4-plans): add addon price snapshot on renewal`.
  Otherwise use the area — `infra`, `ci`, `docs`, `test`.
- Small commits per tracer-bullet slice; imperative, why-focused messages.
- One logical change per commit. Don’t bundle an unrelated refactor into a
  feature commit — call it out and suggest splitting instead.

## Branches & PRs

- Branch per slice: `feat/m4-renewal-snapshot`, `fix/m11-crm-pipeline-filter`.
  Do not commit features directly to `main`.
- PR description states the **module (M1–M13)** and the PRD / `architecture-plan.md`
  section it implements, plus any deliberately deferred scope it does **not** touch
  (plan §13 non-goals).
- PR must satisfy the compliance checklist in `docs/architecture-plan.md` §12.
